## 3.2 Browser Execution Architecture

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle: System startup

    Idle --> Launching: execute_test()
    Launching --> BrowserReady: Browser launched/acquired from pool
    BrowserReady --> ContextCreated: new_context(video, tracing)
    ContextCreated --> PageReady: new_page()
    PageReady --> Executing: Run test steps
    Executing --> Capturing: Capture artifacts
    Capturing --> ContextClosed: Close context (saves video)
    ContextClosed --> BrowserReady: Return browser to pool
    ContextClosed --> Idle: No pending tests

    Executing --> Failed: Test failure
    Failed --> SelfHealing: retry_count < max
    SelfHealing --> ContextCreated: New context for retry
    Failed --> Capturing: Max retries exceeded

    Executing --> TimedOut: Timeout exceeded
    TimedOut --> Capturing: Force artifact capture
    
    BrowserReady --> Recycled: Max contexts reached
    Recycled --> Launching: Launch fresh browser
```

## 3.3 Async Execution Architecture

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant API as FastAPI (async)
    participant WF as LangGraph Workflow (async)
    participant DF as DriverFactory
    participant BP as BrowserPool
    participant CTX as BrowserContext
    participant PG as Page
    participant ART as ArtifactManager
    participant WS as WebSocket

    API->>WF: await agent_app.ainvoke(inputs)
    WF->>DF: await factory.create_driver("playwright")
    DF->>BP: await pool.acquire_browser()
    BP-->>DF: browser instance
    DF-->>WF: PlaywrightDriver

    WF->>WS: emit("execution_started")

    loop For each test script
        WF->>CTX: await browser.new_context(record_video=True)
        CTX->>PG: await context.new_page()
        
        Note over PG: Execute async Playwright steps
        PG->>PG: await page.goto(url)
        PG->>PG: await page.fill(selector, value)
        PG->>PG: await page.click(selector)
        
        alt Test passes
            PG->>ART: await page.screenshot()
            CTX->>ART: await context.tracing.stop()
        else Test fails
            PG->>ART: await page.screenshot(full_page=True)
            CTX->>ART: Save trace + video
            WF->>WS: emit("test_failed", error)
        end
        
        CTX->>CTX: await context.close()
    end

    WF->>BP: await pool.release_browser(browser)
    WF->>WS: emit("execution_completed")
```

## 3.4 Browser Pool Architecture

```python
# Target: backend/automation/browser_pool.py

class BrowserPoolConfig:
    max_browsers: int = 3            # Max concurrent browser instances
    max_contexts_per_browser: int = 10  # Recycle after N contexts
    browser_idle_timeout: int = 300   # Close idle browsers after 5 min
    launch_args: list = [
        "--disable-dev-shm-usage",   # Docker-friendly
        "--disable-gpu",
        "--no-sandbox"
    ]

class BrowserPoolManager:
    """
    Manages a pool of Playwright browser instances.
    
    Lifecycle:
    1. On first request: launch browser, add to pool
    2. On subsequent requests: reuse existing browser via new context
    3. After max_contexts: recycle browser (close + relaunch)
    4. On idle timeout: close browser to free resources
    5. On shutdown: close all browsers gracefully
    """
    
    # Pool state
    _browsers: Dict[str, BrowserSlot]  # id -> {browser, context_count, created_at}
    _semaphore: asyncio.Semaphore      # Limit concurrent browsers
    _playwright: Playwright            # Single playwright instance
    
    async def acquire(self) -> Browser:
        """Get a browser from pool or launch new one."""
        
    async def release(self, browser_id: str):
        """Return browser to pool, increment context count."""
        
    async def _recycle(self, browser_id: str):
        """Close and relaunch a browser that hit max contexts."""
        
    async def shutdown(self):
        """Gracefully close all browsers and playwright instance."""
```

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph "Browser Pool Manager"
        SEM[Semaphore - max 3]
        
        subgraph "Slot 1"
            B1[Chromium Browser #1]
            C1A[Context A - Test TC-001]
            C1B[Context B - Test TC-002]
        end
        
        subgraph "Slot 2"
            B2[Chromium Browser #2]
            C2A[Context C - Test TC-003]
        end
        
        subgraph "Slot 3 - Idle"
            B3[Chromium Browser #3]
            IDLE[Idle - timeout: 4:30]
        end
    end
    
    REQ[New Test Request] --> SEM
    SEM -->|slot available| B1
    SEM -->|slot available| B2
    SEM -->|all busy| WAIT[Wait for release]
```

## 3.5 Artifact Pipeline Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph "During Execution"
        A[BrowserContext Created] -->|record_video=path| B[Auto Video Recording]
        A -->|tracing.start| C[Trace Recording]
        D[Page Interactions] -->|on failure| E[page.screenshot]
        D -->|on each step| F[Optional step screenshots]
    end

    subgraph "After Context Close"
        B --> G[video.path → saved MP4/WebM]
        C --> H[tracing.stop → trace.zip]
        E --> I[screenshot.png]
    end

    subgraph "Artifact Manager"
        G --> J[ArtifactManager.save_video]
        H --> K[ArtifactManager.save_trace]
        I --> L[ArtifactManager.save_screenshot]
        J & K & L --> M[test_results/test_id/]
        M --> N[Update DB: test_executions]
    end
```

**Key improvement**: Playwright's built-in video recording replaces the entire `video_recorder.py` (83 lines of OpenCV + threading code) with a single parameter: `record_video={"dir": "path/"}`.

## 3.6 Target Class Hierarchy

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class BaseDriver {
        <<abstract>>
        +engine_name: str
        +launch() → Browser
        +create_context(config) → ExecutionContext
        +close()
        +screenshot(path) → str
        +get_browser_info() → dict
    }

    class PlaywrightDriver {
        -_playwright: Playwright
        -_browser: Browser
        -_pool: BrowserPoolManager
        +launch()
        +create_context(config) → PlaywrightExecutionContext
        +close()
        +screenshot(path) → str
    }

    class SeleniumDriver {
        -_driver: WebDriver
        +launch()
        +create_context(config) → SeleniumExecutionContext
        +close()
        +screenshot(path) → str
    }

    class DriverFactory {
        +create(engine: str, config: dict) → BaseDriver
        +get_default_engine() → str
    }

    class ExecutionContext {
        <<abstract>>
        +page: Any
        +navigate(url)
        +fill(selector, value)
        +click(selector)
        +get_text(selector) → str
        +wait_for(selector, state, timeout)
        +screenshot(path) → str
        +close()
    }

    class PlaywrightExecutionContext {
        -_context: BrowserContext
        -_page: Page
        -_tracing: bool
        +start_tracing()
        +stop_tracing(path)
        +video_path() → str
    }

    class ArtifactManager {
        +save_screenshot(context, test_id) → str
        +save_video(context, test_id) → str
        +save_trace(context, test_id) → str
        +cleanup_old_artifacts(days)
    }

    class BrowserPoolManager {
        -_browsers: Dict
        -_semaphore: Semaphore
        +acquire() → Browser
        +release(browser_id)
        +shutdown()
    }

    BaseDriver <|-- PlaywrightDriver
    BaseDriver <|-- SeleniumDriver
    DriverFactory --> BaseDriver
    PlaywrightDriver --> BrowserPoolManager
    ExecutionContext <|-- PlaywrightExecutionContext
    PlaywrightDriver --> ArtifactManager
```

## 3.7 Execution State Machine

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> QUEUED: Test submitted

    QUEUED --> PREPARING: Worker picks up
    PREPARING --> BROWSER_ACQUIRED: Pool returns browser
    BROWSER_ACQUIRED --> CONTEXT_READY: Context + page created
    
    CONTEXT_READY --> RUNNING: Script execution starts
    RUNNING --> STEP_EXECUTING: Each test step
    STEP_EXECUTING --> STEP_EXECUTING: Next step
    STEP_EXECUTING --> RUNNING: Step completed
    
    RUNNING --> PASSED: All steps pass
    RUNNING --> FAILED: Assertion failure
    RUNNING --> ERROR: Unexpected error
    RUNNING --> TIMED_OUT: Timeout exceeded
    RUNNING --> CANCELLED: User cancellation
    
    PASSED --> COLLECTING_ARTIFACTS: Save screenshots/video/trace
    FAILED --> COLLECTING_ARTIFACTS
    ERROR --> COLLECTING_ARTIFACTS
    TIMED_OUT --> COLLECTING_ARTIFACTS
    CANCELLED --> CLEANUP
    
    COLLECTING_ARTIFACTS --> COMPLETED: Results persisted
    CLEANUP --> COMPLETED
    
    COMPLETED --> [*]
    
    FAILED --> HEALING: retry_count < max AND auto_heal=true
    HEALING --> CONTEXT_READY: New context for retry
```

## 3.8 WebSocket Streaming Architecture (Unchanged)

> [!NOTE]
> The WebSocket layer requires **zero changes**. It emits abstract execution events (started, progress, completed, agent_log) that are completely engine-agnostic. The `ExecutionEventEmitter` class works identically with Playwright.

The only enhancement opportunity is adding Playwright-specific trace URLs to completion events:

```python
# Enhanced completion event
await emitter.emit_completed(
    execution_id=execution_id,
    status="failed",
    duration=12.5,
    error_message="Element not found",
    trace_url="/api/agent/executions/{id}/trace",  # NEW: Playwright trace
    video_url="/api/agent/executions/{id}/video"   # Already exists
)
```

